153,10747,374,894,6716,315,15279,11067,315,264,5792,12371,6113,448,3108,315,220,21,8153,30,17399,697,4226,304,44548,17855,1352,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nHow many units apart is any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with side of 6 units? Express your answer in simplest radical form.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b0c864f27287856360fda3e11656a529cc49721449efde5d17ce3ded82e3d3d5"},"seconds":19.932406187057495,"seed":348978479180722424,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem of finding how many units apart any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with a side length of 6 units are, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the Structure of the Hexagon:**\n   A regular hexagon can be divided into 6 equilateral triangles. Each side of the hexagon serves as a side of two such triangles.\n\n2. **Calculate the Height of an Equilateral Triangle:**\n   Since each side of the hexagon is 6 units, each of the equilateral triangles has sides of 6 units. The height \\( h \\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\( s \\) can be found using the formula:\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} s\n   \\]\n   For \\( s = 6 \\):\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 6 = 3\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the Distance Between Parallel Sides:**\n   In a regular hexagon, the distance between any pair of parallel sides is equal to the height of two equilateral triangles (since the hexagon can be split into two rows of these triangles). Thus, the distance \\( d \\) between parallel sides is:\n   \\[\n   d = 2 \\times 3\\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the units apart any pair of parallel sides of the regular hexagon is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
